  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records collectively establish several relevant ingredients: powder consolidation and sintering near 1400 °C, oxygen-sensitive processing and oxygen-derived strengthening, in-situ additive alloying of refractory elemental powder mixtures to dense single-BCC material, the BCC character and high-temperature utility of HfNbTaTiZr-type alloys, and the use of coatings or protective oxides to mitigate oxidation. However, none discloses hydride-based extrusion ink, hydrogen de-binding, sequential hydride decomposition governed by formation enthalpies, titanium-sponge oxygen gettering, controlled interstitial oxygen uptake, quench retention of metastable beta-BCC, or a self-healing silicide coating. Thus the literature points in the general direction, but combining these elements into the later paper's specific processing and mechanistic scheme would require substantial new ideas."
